For a tile-based grid game where the player navigates corridors and cannot pass through walls (any theme — maze chase, collectibles, fleeing pursuers after a power pickup): define state.maze[row][col] at build time (0=corridor, 1=wall, 2=door, 3=exit). Position the player by tile coords (state.player.tx, ty); derive pixel coords (px=tx*TILE_SIZE) at draw time. Chasers live in state.chasers[] or state.enemies[] (not title-locked). Movement: on keydown, check maze[nextTy][nextTx] !== 1 BEFORE applying. Expose collectiblesLeft/dotsRemaining and vulnerableTimer/powerTimer for probes.
state: maze[r][c]; player{tx,ty,dir}; chasers[]{tx,ty,mode}; collectiblesLeft; vulnerableTimer; score; over
order: input sets desired dir -> at tile centers accept turn if open -> check maze[nextTy][nextTx]!==1 BEFORE moving -> move/wrap/clamp -> enemy steps -> tile events (eat/dig/bomb) -> draw maze, items, actors
traps:
- moving then checking walls: validate the target tile first or the player enters walls
